          "empirical_p_one_sided_greater": 0.000999000999000999,
          "n_permutations": 1000
        }
      },
      "narrowing_notes": "CAF/M2-defined niche centers (top-quartile CAF and M2 spots; n = 372) showed higher, not lower, neighbor T-cell scores compared with matched background spots (neighbor mean difference = 0.18, d = 0.43, p = 6.8e-07). CAF_M2_niche labels were strongly spatially clustered (observed niche\u2013niche neighbor fraction = 0.24, permutation p (greater than random) = 0.001), indicating coherent CAF/M2-rich regions. However, because these regions are associated with local T-cell enrichment rather than depletion under the current quartile thresholds and neighborhood definition, the data do not support the specific immunosuppressive niche pattern as stated. Alternative threshold choices or finer spatial scales may be needed to reconcile CAF/M2 enrichment with T-cell exclusion."
